# ACT ONE

= A windbound evening. Two old friends andalampthat won'tstaylit.

# SCENE 1

A single oil lamp on awooden table, centre stage. ELENA sitsbeside it, reading.The light flickers. Outside, awind thathas been blowingfor three days is somehow louder now.

ELENA
(without looking up)
You're back early.

MARCUS enters from the wings, brushing snow from his coat.

MARCUS
The road's closed past the bridge.
ELENA
Then sit down before you melt on the carpet.

MARCUS sits opposite her. The lamp gutters. Both lookatit,then at each other.

ELENA
Don't.
MARCUS
I haven't done anything.
ELENA
You were about to.

A long pause. The wind eases for a moment,andinthegapMARCUSspeaks more quietly than he means to.

MARCUS
I had a letter today.
ELENA
(turning a page)
From whom.
MARCUS
You know from whom.

ELENA closes the book. She does not look at him.

ELENA
What did it say.
MARCUS
That she'swell.Thatshe'scomingbackinthespring. That shewould
like to see us. Both of us.

= Elena considers throwing the book.

.ELENA

"Both of us."MARCUSThat's what it said.

The lamp goes outcompletely.Neitherofthemmoves.AfteramomentELENA strikes amatch.Thelightcomesback,smallerthanbefore.

# SCENE 2

The lamp has gone outagain,properlythistime.ELENAisalone,standingat the window.Thewindhasstopped.Thesilence isworse.

ELENA
(to the dark)
I knew you would.

She does not turn when MARCUS enters quietly behind her.

MARCUS
Knew I would what.
ELENA
Write back.

A beat.

MARCUS
I haven't yet.
ELENA
But you will.

He doesn't answer. She finally turns.

ELENA
I'm not asking you to choose.
MARCUS
I know.
ELENA
I'm telling you that you already have.

Lights fade.

# ACT TWO

= Same room. The thaw, and what it brings up out of theground.

# SCENE 1

= Test

The same room, mid-morning. Sunlightwheretherehasbeennoneforthreedays. ELENA pours tea forone.Thelampisstillonthetable, unlit,spotless. ThereisnosignofMARCUS.

She lifts the cup. She does not drink.

ELENA
(softly)
Alright.

A KNOCK at the door. She does not move.

ELENA
(to herself)
Alright.

Another knock. She setsthecupdownwithoutspillingitandcrossesto the door. Shedoesnotopenit.

ELENA
(through the door)
Tell her the road's open now.

She returns to the table and sits in MARCUS's chair.

End of play.

